// Measurement scenario for docs/measurements/2026-08-24-stack-danger-changes.md.
//
// The worst-case reading of "a fresh player's first stack bottom": a
// level-1 player with nothing equipped and no party at all, standing at
// the bottom of the shallowest possible stack (depth 2, the minimum
// STACK_FRAMES_MIN) under a Mainframe sector, and rousing the guardian.
// Since pick_lair_species draws unconditionally from the biome's apex pool
// now (APEX_ENTRY_STEP no longer gates a Lair), and Mainframe's apex pool
// is non-empty (overseer, wintermute both list it), this fight is always
// against a hand-authored apex species rather than a rolled-up ordinary one.
(
    player: Fresh(level: 1, zone: 1),
    encounter: Some(Lair(biome: Mainframe, depth: 2)),
    reps: 300,
    seed: 5001,
)
